  "full_response": "Designing RESTful APIs involves following a set of best practices to ensure they are scalable, maintainable, and easy to use. Here are some key best practices:\n\n### 1. **Use Nouns Instead of Verbs in Endpoints**\n   - RESTful APIs should use nouns to represent resources, not verbs.\n   - **Good:** `/users`, `/users/{id}`\n   - **Bad:** `/getUsers`, `/createUser`\n\n### 2. **Use Plural Nouns for Collections**\n   - Use plural nouns for collections to maintain consistency.\n   - **Example:** `/users` instead of `/user`\n\n### 3. **Use HTTP Methods Correctly**\n   - **GET:** Retrieve a resource.\n   - **POST:** Create a resource.\n   - **PUT:** Update/replace a resource (full update).\n   - **PATCH:** Partially update a resource.\n   - **DELETE:** Remove a resource.\n\n### 4. **Use Proper HTTP Status Codes**\n   - **200 OK:** Successful GET, PUT, or PATCH.\n   - **201 Created:** Successful POST (resource created).\n   - **204 No Content:** Successful DELETE.\n   - **400 Bad Request:** Invalid input.\n   - **401 Unauthorized:** Authentication failed.\n   - **403 Forbidden:** Authenticated but not allowed.\n   - **404 Not Found:** Resource doesn’t exist.\n   - **500 Internal Server Error:** Server-side error.\n\n### 5. **Version Your API**\n   - Include the API version in the URL or headers to avoid breaking changes.\n   - **Example:** `/v1/users` or `Accept: application/vnd.company.api.v1+json`\n\n### 6. **Use Query Parameters for Filtering, Sorting, and Pagination**\n   - **Filtering:** `/users?role=admin`\n   - **Sorting:** `/users?sort=-createdAt` (descending)\n   - **Pagination:** `/users?page=2&limit=10`\n\n### 7. **Use HATEOAS (Hypermedia as the Engine of Application State)**\n   - Include links to related resources in responses to guide clients.\n   - **Example:**\n     ```json\n     {\n       \"id\": 1,\n       \"name\": \"John Doe\",\n       \"_links\": {\n         \"self\": { \"href\": \"/users/1\" },\n         \"orders\":",
